{"findings":[{"finding":"REQ-13 forces any quantity up to a minimum of 1, but REQ-14 caps it at the part's stock, so a cart line whose part now has 0 stock has two contradictory required outcomes (1 vs 0).","reqId":"REQ-13","rubric":1,"severity":"high"},{"finding":"REQ-39 removes lines with 0 available stock based on ASM-25, an assumption the spec added itself; it contradicts the accepted ASM-3, which says affected lines are lowered to the available stock and the cart is kept.","reqId":"REQ-39","rubric":1,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"NFR-1 requires a 2 s p95 on all three screens at 1,000 concurrent users, but I-8 covers only 5,000 parts and ASM-16 says 1,000 users in total; it also goes beyond REQ-38, which covers only the Find parts screen.","reqId":"NFR-1","rubric":4,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"Retrying after a network error (REQ-24) has no duplicate-submission or idempotency protection, so an order the server already saved can be placed twice.","reqId":"REQ-24","rubric":2,"severity":"high"},{"finding":"The cart keeps a copy of the unit price in local storage while REQ-20 charges the current server price, and no requirement covers telling the buyer when the price has changed, so the total shown can differ from the total saved.","reqId":"REQ-16","rubric":2,"severity":"high"},{"finding":"The 401 path is defined only for the API; nothing says what the portal does when the session expires during browsing or checkout (redirect to login, keep the cart, etc.).","reqId":"REQ-26","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"The cart is keyed by buyer ID in local storage, but the spec never says how the client gets the buyer ID, or what happens to the stored cart on sign-out or on a shared device.","reqId":"REQ-16","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"There is a brands endpoint but no source or endpoint for the category list, and no defined response for an unknown category or brand value.","reqId":"REQ-5","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"No behaviour is defined for an invalid or out-of-range page parameter (page=0, page=abc, a page past the last one).","reqId":"REQ-2","rubric":2,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"No behaviour is defined for an unknown status filter value, and the set of valid statuses (including Cancelled and an 'All' option) is never listed.","reqId":"REQ-29","rubric":2,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"The timeline only defines Placed → Packed → Dispatched → Delivered, so it is undefined what an order in Cancelled status shows.","reqId":"REQ-31","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"Unknown part numbers, quantities above 99 and a missing delivery option are rejected in the EARS text but none of them has an acceptance criterion.","reqId":"REQ-21","rubric":2,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"AC-20.2 is checked by reading the orders and order_lines tables directly instead of a public API response such as GET /api/orders/{orderNumber}.","reqId":"REQ-20","rubric":3,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"AC-25.1 checks the parts table row directly instead of the stock value returned by GET /api/parts.","reqId":"REQ-25","rubric":3,"severity":"low"}],"note":"No OpenAI key: critic ran on claude-opus-5-5 (same family as the implementer)"}